{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Dwell in the land which I say to you.</b> And afterward He said immediately, ״גּוּר בָּאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת״ — and if so, what is the meaning of what He said, ״אֲשֶׁר אֹמַר אֵלֶיךָ״, which implies that after some time He will say to him in which land he shall dwell, when He immediately and forthwith told him which land it is? And this is a puzzling thing in the verse. And what seems close in my eyes to say regarding this is that He prevented him from going outside the Land, because there the Shechinah does not reveal itself, and if so, He could not say anything to him there in prophecy according to the need of the moment. Therefore, ״שְׁכוֹן בָּאָרֶץ״ — in the land where the revelation of My Shechinah is, and there ״אֹמַר אֵלֶיךָ״ at the time that I wish to say to you something in prophecy. And through this what He said at the outset is settled — ״שְׁכוֹן בָּאָרֶץ״ — and afterward He said ״גּוּר בָּאָרֶץ״, for ״שְׁכוֹן״ implies more of a permanent dwelling than ״גּוּר״, which is an expression of sojourning: for from the aspect of acquiring spiritual perfection in this Land, you shall dwell in it as a permanent resident (תוֹשָׁב); but from the aspect of acquiring physical blessings, you shall be in it as a sojourner (גֵּר). This is what He said, ״גּוּר בָּאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת״ and so forth, for everything said after it speaks of promises of physicality. And this is what it says: ״גֵּר וְתוֹשָׁב אָנֹכִי עִמָּכֶם״ (Genesis 23:4) — a sojourner from one aspect, and a permanent resident from another."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:19.446651908Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}